Hello Jay and Celine, 

CDFs for exon arrays are "unsupported" and a bit messy indeed. 
They include control and background probesets that are represented as MM
or single-probe-probesets. 
This makes raw CDFs not useful for BioConductor, and probably that's why
they are not included in the BioC metadata packages. 

The package versions of CDFs with BKG and control probesets removed you
can find at:
http://xmap.picr.man.ac.uk/cdf

There are some other attempts to solve the issue, it is currently
discussed also on affy-aroma list. 

Cheers,
Michal 
  

